# Google Drive support. Copy this file to `.env.local` (git-ignored) to use it on
# the dev server; the deployed page reads the same three values from the
# repository's Actions secrets, injected by .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#
# Leave them unset and the site keeps its local file picker — the Drive button
# then explains that the setup is missing rather than doing nothing.
#
# These are not secrets in the cryptographic sense: Vite inlines them into the
# bundle, which is served publicly, so they are readable in the deployed page.
# Keeping them out of the repository still buys a clean git history and lets you
# rotate one without a commit. What actually protects them is the origin
# restriction you set in step 3 and step 4 below.
#
# One-time setup, at https://console.cloud.google.com:
#
#   1. Create a project. Under "APIs & Services > Library", enable both the
#      "Google Drive API" and the "Google Picker API". Enable nothing else on
#      this project — a leaked API key only costs money if it also unlocks a
#      billed API such as Maps or Vision.
#   2. "OAuth consent screen": User type External, fill in the app name and your
#      own email, and add your own address under "Test users". No verification
#      review is needed: the scope this app asks for (drive.file) is not a
#      sensitive one, because it only ever reaches the files you pick yourself.
#   3. "Credentials > Create credentials > OAuth client ID", type Web
#      application. Under "Authorised JavaScript origins" add both
#      http://localhost:5173 (the dev server) and https://cluneau.github.io
#      (the deployed page — Google takes no path, so the origin covers the whole
#      site). That allowlist is what stops the client ID working anywhere else.
#   4. "Credentials > Create credentials > API key". Restrict it to those same
#      two origins under "Websites", and to the Picker API under "API
#      restrictions".
#   5. The project number is on the console's dashboard, beside the project name.
#      The Picker needs it to know which app it is granting the picked file to.
#
# Then, for the deployed page: Settings > Secrets and variables > Actions > New
# repository secret, once per value, named GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_API_KEY and
# GOOGLE_APP_ID.

VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
